WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:15.512
Aunt Judy carried a tote bag.

2
00:00:15.513 --> 00:00:19.779
"Where are you going?" asked Emmy.

3
00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:24.199
"I'm going on an adventure," said Aunt Judy.

4
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.066
She winked at the kids.

5
00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:37.274
"It's a mystery adventure."

6
00:00:37.275 --> 00:00:42.636
The kids followed Aunt Judy to the kitchen.

7
00:00:42.637 --> 00:00:47.591
She got two apples.

8
00:00:47.592 --> 00:00:52.864
"Adventures make me hungry," said Aunt Judy.

9
00:00:52.865 --> 00:00:56.981
"Are you going far?" asked Harry.

10
00:00:56.982 --> 00:01:01.056
Aunt Judy looked out the window.

11
00:01:01.057 --> 00:01:07.646
"As far as you can imagine," she said.

12
00:01:07.647 --> 00:01:15.829
The kids followed Aunt Judy to her closet.

13
00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:19.412
She got her shoes.

14
00:01:19.413 --> 00:01:24.681
"But it's not too far to walk," she said.

15
00:01:24.682 --> 00:01:29.041
Aunt Judy put on a sweater.

16
00:01:29.042 --> 00:01:34.471
"It's an outside adventure."

17
00:01:34.472 --> 00:01:39.399
"Will you meet wild animals?" asked Oliver.

18
00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:43.241
"Hmm," said Aunt Judy.

19
00:01:43.242 --> 00:01:47.332
"It's possible."

20
00:01:47.333 --> 00:01:50.471
Emmy looked worried.

21
00:01:50.472 --> 00:01:54.041
"Will there be danger?" she asked.

22
00:01:54.042 --> 00:02:00.076
"Oh yes," said Aunt Judy.

23
00:02:00.077 --> 00:02:06.683
"Mystery adventures are always dangerous."

24
00:02:06.684 --> 00:02:12.576
Aunt Judy put on her hat.

25
00:02:12.577 --> 00:02:15.835
"But don't worry," she said.

26
00:02:15.836 --> 00:02:24.668
"I'll meet new friends."

27
00:02:24.669 --> 00:02:27.832
Oliver hugged Aunt Judy.

28
00:02:27.833 --> 00:02:31.235
"We'll miss you," he said.

29
00:02:31.236 --> 00:02:37.399
"You can all come with me," said Aunt Judy.

30
00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:42.312
She pulled something from her bag.

31
00:02:42.313 --> 00:02:46.503
It was a book.

32
00:02:46.504 --> 00:02:53.111
"I'm going outside to read."

33
00:02:53.112 --> 00:02:57.238
"I want to come!" said Oliver.

34
00:02:57.239 --> 00:03:01.881
"Me too!" said Emmy and Harry.

35
00:03:01.882 --> 00:03:10.172
They all ran to get their books.
